Hi Tomas,

Thanks so much for your reply. That's a great idea, I haven't given any thought to trying JAGs.  It's also good to hear that you're having similar problems! I tried some of my data in the 'unmarked' gdistamp package, but the models took a very long time and some of them (I think when I tried to use the half-normal key function) never did converge, which is what drove me to try BUGs in the first place.  It's a good idea to try with a constant pA value, though.

Thanks very much, and good luck with your models,

Lucretia

