Hey Tomas and Lucretia-

I found when we combined hierarchical distance sampling and removal sampling in a Bayesian model that JAGS was the only program that would really work for it (and it does still take awhile to converge).  There isn't a canned spatial autocorrelation function in JAGS, but I can send you some JAGS code for an exponential decay function that will behave similarly if you're interested (just need to manipulate the decay rate to include only adjacent units if that's what you're after).  The supplemental file for our Auk paper includes JAGS code that doesn't rely on the '1's trick' if that might also be useful (http://www.bioone.org/doi/abs/10.1642/AUK-14-11.1)?

Courtney-

